# forge/sheen/glowing: the glowing tell (28.7, D28): the engine already writes a glowing alloy's seams (N) in Glow from
# T4; this tile lights them evenly when a style draws its seams at step 1: Glow 2 with a Glow 3 hot point every fourth
# cell along any line, an ember line, never a neon tube.
# FORGE-MARKS, forge i2 (tools: emb_P2c/forge/areas/FORGE-MARKS/tools2/mk2.py). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# SHEEN TELL (STYLE_P2 28.7; asks FORGE-DOLL to lay it as a cut tile after the cut when the body's sheen is this one):
# the iridescent rows recolour alternate courses of the row cuts to Metal 2 keeping the step (P2C_CONTRACTS 3c: an
# iridescent alloy's Metal 2 is its hue-turned ramp, so the courses alternate two hues), keyed by the cut.
use person
role overlay sheen.glowing
# (FINISH wave-2 fix r2, D79) RESERVE: the engine writes a glowing alloy's seams in Glow from T4 (flag sheen-glowing, D28/D40 glowseams); no resolver asks `overlay sheen.glowing`. Kept drawn, listed, never deleted (D49).
tags tile overlay reserve
on-region N
legend g glow 2
legend ! glow 3

# (envelope r1, FORGE-MATERIAL; A7, B8 "never a checker") the seam's bright beads as 2 px runs: a horizontal seam reads
# g!!g, a vertical one ! ! g g, so the glass's seams pulse in short bars, never a checker of single sparks.
view D key rest origin 0 0
|g!!g
|g!!g
|gggg
|gggg
